public class TreePlantation {
    private double soilQuality;
    private double climate;
    private double landAvailability;
    public TreePlantation(double soilQuality, double climate, double landAvailability) {
        this.soilQuality = soilQuality;
        this.climate = climate;
        this.landAvailability = landAvailability;
    }
    public double calculateIdealNumberOfTrees() {
        double idealNumberOfTrees = (soilQuality * climate * landAvailability) / 100;
        return idealNumberOfTrees;
    }
}
```
This code snippet takes in three factors - soil quality, climate, and land availability - and calculates the ideal number of trees that should be planted in the given area. The formula used to calculate the ideal number of trees is a simple multiplication of these three factors, divided by 100.
