One possible solution to solve this puzzle using Java code is to create an array of 6 machines and an array of 8 products, and then use nested loops to iterate over all possible combinations of machines and products. For each combination, we can check if it satisfies all the given clues and eliminate any invalid combinations until we find the correct solution.
Here is a sample Java code that implements this approach:
```
public class FactoryPuzzleSolver {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        char[] machines = {'A', 'B', 'C', 'D', 'E', 'F'};
        int[] products = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8};
        char[] machineLabels = new char[8];
        // iterate over all possible combinations of machines and products
        for (char machine : machines) {
            for (int product : products) {
                // check if the current combination satisfies all the clues
                if (isValid(machineLabels, machine, product)) {
                    // add the current machine label to the array of machine labels
                    machineLabels[product - 1] = machine;
                }
            }
        }
        // print the solution
        for (int i = 0; i < 8; i++) {
            System.out.println("Machine " + machineLabels[i] + " produces product " + (i + 1));
        }
    }
    // check if the current combination satisfies all the clues
    private static boolean isValid(char[] machineLabels, char machine, int product) {
        // check clues 1, 2, 3, 4, and 6
        if ((machine == 'B' && (product == 5 || product == 6)) ||
                ((machine == 'A' || machine == 'D' || machine == 'E') && product % 2 == 0) ||
                ((machine == 'B' || machine == 'C' || machine == 'F') && product % 2 != 0) ||
                (machine == 'A' && product != 7) ||
                (machine == 'C' && (product == 2 || product == 3 || product == 4)) ||
                (machine == 'F' && !(product == 2 || product == 4 || product == 6 || product == 8))) {
            return false;
        }
        // check clue 5
        for (int i = 0; i < machineLabels.length; i++) {
            if (machineLabels[i] == 'C' && (i + 1) == product && (i + 1) != 2 && (i + 1) != 3 && (i + 1) != 4) {
                return false;
            }
        }
        return true;
    }
}
```
