To generate twenty randomized eight-character words that start with the letter "M" and alternate between two different consonants, with the last character being a vowel, you can use the following HTML code:
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<body>
<button onclick="generateWords()">Generate Words</button>
<p id="words"></p>
<script>
function generateWords() {
  let words = [];
  let consonants = ['B', 'C', 'D', 'F', 'G', 'H', 'J', 'K', 'L', 'N', 'P', 'Q', 'R', 'S', 'T', 'V', 'W', 'X', 'Y', 'Z'];
  let vowels = ['A', 'E', 'I', 'O', 'U'];
  for (let i = 0; i < 20; i++) {
    let word = 'M';
    let consonant1 = consonants[Math.floor(Math.random() * consonants.length)];
    let consonant2 = consonants[Math.floor(Math.random() * consonants.length)];
    let vowel = vowels[Math.floor(Math.random() * vowels.length)];
    for (let j = 1; j < 8; j++) {
      if (j % 2 == 1) {
        word += consonant1;
      } else {
        word += consonant2;
      }
    }
    word += vowel;
    words.push(word);
  }
  document.getElementById("words").innerHTML = words.join(", ");
}
</script>
</body>
</html>
```
This code creates a button that, when clicked, generates twenty randomized eight-character words that start with the letter "M" and alternate between two different consonants, with the last character being a vowel. 
The code first defines two arrays, `consonants` and `vowels`, which contain all the consonants and vowels, respectively. It then loops through twenty times and generates a word for each iteration. 
For each word, the code starts with the letter "M" and randomly selects two consonants and a vowel from the `consonants` and `vowels` arrays. It then loops through the remaining seven characters of the word and alternates between the two consonants.
Finally, the code adds the vowel to the end of the word and adds the word to the `words` array. The `words` array is then joined into a string and displayed in the `p` element with the `id` of "words".

