        for (int j = i + 1; j < n; j++)
        {
            double s = A[j, i] / A[i, i];
            for (int k = i; k <= n; k++)
            {
                A[j, k] = A[j, k] - s * A[i, k];
            }
            b[j] = b[j] - s * b[i];
        }
    }
    // back substitution
    double[] x = new double[n];
    for (int i = n - 1; i >= 0; i--)
    {
        double sum = 0.0;
        for (int j = i + 1; j < n; j++)
        {
            sum += A[i, j] * x[j];
        }
        x[i] = (b[i] - sum) / A[i, i];
    }
    return x;
}
```
Note that this code assumes that the equations of the planes are given in the form `ax + by + cz = d`, where `a`, `b`, `c`, and `d` are constants. If your equations are in a different form, you may need to modify the code accordingly.

